"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[58900],{658900:e=>{e.exports='# Find a Datasource\n\nHow to find or retrieve a **datasource** by ID or by name. Use when the user asks to view, get, or modify a specific datasource.\n\n## User provides a datasource ID\n\nDatasource IDs are random-generated and **start with `ds-`** (e.g. `ds-abc123xyz`). When the user gives an ID explicitly or one that starts with `ds-`, call `apiGetLakewatchResourceById` with `resourceType: "datasource"` and `resourceId` set to that ID.\n\n```json\n{\n  "thoughts": "User provided datasource ID \'ds-abc123xyz\'. Retrieving the datasource directly.",\n  "resourceType": "datasource",\n  "resourceId": "ds-abc123xyz"\n}\n```\n\n## User provides a datasource name\n\nWhen the user references a datasource by human-readable name (e.g. “cloudtrail logs”):\n\n1. Call **apiListLakewatchDatasources** with `thoughts` and `limit` (e.g. 100).\n2. Search the list for a datasource matching the name: check `metadata.name`, display name, description; match case-insensitively; allow spaces vs. hyphens vs. underscores.\n3. Extract the ID (e.g. from `metadata.name`).\n4. Call **apiGetLakewatchResourceById** with `resourceType: "datasource"` and that `resourceId`.\n\n**Multiple matches**: Present all with ID, display name, and description; ask the user which one they want.\n\n**No match**: Tell the user no datasource matched; suggest listing all datasources or creating a new one.\n'}}]);
